Step 1: Upload trained model to S3

Go to Amazon S3

Open AWS Console → search S3
Create bucket (if not created)
Upload your model file

Example:

model.tar.gz
model.pkl
model.joblib
model.pt
model.onnx

Typical path: s3://my-bucket/model.tar.gz


Step 2: Create Model in SageMaker

Create a notebook instance (scroll down see iam role then attach s3fullaccess policy to its iam)
open notebook instance -> create a inference.py file and conda python3 file


---------------
inference.py:
---------------
import joblib
import os

def model_fn(model_dir):
    return joblib.load(os.path.join(model_dir, "model.pkl"))

def predict_fn(input_data, model):
    return model.predict(input_data)


----------
ML.ipynb:
----------
from sagemaker.sklearn.model import SKLearnModel
import sagemaker

role = sagemaker.get_execution_role()

model = SKLearnModel(
    model_data="s3://pretrained-model-2003/model.tar.gz",
    role=role,
    entry_point="inference.py",
    framework_version="1.2-1"
)

predictor = model.deploy(
    instance_type="ml.t2.medium",
    initial_instance_count=1,
    endpoint_name="pretrained-endpoint"
)

print("Endpoint created!")
